# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Rust / Axum

> Generated: {{GENERATION_DATE}} | Claude Craft v{{VERSION}}

## What (Stack & Structure)

**Stack**: Rust {{RUST_VERSION}} (edition 2024), Axum {{AXUM_VERSION}}, Tokio, SQLx, Tower

### Project Structure
```
Cargo.toml              # Workspace manifest (shared dependencies and lints)
rust-toolchain.toml     # Pinned toolchain, rustfmt and clippy components
crates/
├── domain/             # Entities, value objects, ports (traits) - no axum, no sqlx
├── application/        # Use cases (one use case = one type with an `execute`)
├── infrastructure/     # Adapters: SQLx repositories, HTTP clients, clock, mail
└── api/                # Binary: Router, handlers, extractors, middleware, AppError
migrations/             # SQLx migrations (versioned SQL)
.sqlx/                  # Offline query metadata (committed)
tests/                  # Integration tests (Router + oneshot, #[sqlx::test])
deny.toml               # cargo-deny policy (advisories, licenses, bans, sources)
```

## Why (Purpose & Organization)

### Architecture: layered / hexagonal, enforced by crate boundaries
- **domain**: business rules, no framework dependency (checked by `Cargo.toml`)
- **application**: use cases orchestrating domain objects through ports
- **infrastructure**: adapters implementing the ports (SQLx, HTTP clients)
- **api**: translates HTTP to use cases and back (extractors, `AppError`, middleware)
- A small service may start as a single crate with modules; split when boundaries hurt

See `rules/02-architecture-rust.md` for complete patterns.

### Critical Rules
| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` | Memory safety guaranteed by the compiler |
| `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` + `cargo fmt --check` | Code quality and consistent style |
| No `unwrap()` / `expect()` on request paths | A panic must never be a response |
| SQLx bind parameters only | SQL injection prevention |
| `cargo deny check` + `cargo audit` | Supply-chain and RustSec advisories gate |
| 80%+ coverage (cargo-llvm-cov) | Quality assurance |

## How (Commands & Workflows)

### Development Commands
```bash
docker compose exec app cargo build                  # Build
docker compose exec app cargo run -p api             # Run the server
{{CACHE_CLEAR_COMMAND}}                              # Clear build cache
docker compose exec app cargo nextest run            # Run tests
docker compose exec app cargo fmt --check            # Formatting
docker compose exec app cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
```

### Quality Pipeline
```bash
docker compose exec app cargo fmt --check                                    # Style
docker compose exec app cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings            # Lints
docker compose exec app cargo nextest run                                    # Tests
docker compose exec app cargo llvm-cov nextest --fail-under-lines 80         # Coverage
docker compose exec app cargo deny check                                     # Policy
docker compose exec app cargo audit                                          # RustSec
docker compose exec app cargo sqlx prepare --check --workspace               # Offline metadata
```

### Development Workflow
1. **Analyze** - Read code, understand domain (`rules/01-workflow-analysis.md`)
2. **TDD** - Write test -> Implement -> Refactor
3. **Quality** - Run the quality pipeline inside the container
4. **Commit** - Conventional Commits format

